    "updated_at": "2024-01-11T18:41:43Z",
    "body": "This was discussed during a WHATNOT call in the context of #9065. One use case for inheritance is to allow authors to turn off spellcheck for the whole document by setting the attribute to `false` on the document element. As currently spec'ed, if authors want to also turn off the feature in shadow trees, they would have to explicitly set the `spellcheck` attribute inside each shadow tree. If inheritance worked across shadow boundaries, they would be able to realize this intent more simply.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
